  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">East Africa Accountability Micro-grant partner initiative 2013/14</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving accountability across our programmes is a corporate priority for CAFOD. The overall purpose of the Accountability Micro-Grant Partner Initiative is to enable our partners to implement new and improved ways of working that support accountability to the communities they work with, as well as strengthening their organisational accountability systems and practices.
 
A total of &#xA3;15,248 has been allocated to East Africa to support  four partners whose concepts were successful. The breakdown of the grant is as follows
Diocese of Moroto            &#xA3;6,673.00
St John Sports Society     &#xA3;2,215.00
Archdiocese of  Gulu        &#xA3;3,000.00
Archdiocese of Mombasa  &#xA3;3,360.00</narrative>
  </description>
